caches: the downloads 0089 left go without a staging buffer

Three more places threw when the pool refused a download:

Nx2CopyListPages takes no copy of the page. copy_writes falls behind writes, so reads of that page
report Unknown and drain the split, as for a page without a copy.

CommitAsyncFlushes drops the image downloads of that batch. They run ahead of a read that may not
come. The entries stay in committed_downloads, marked dropped, because one may hold a deleted image
alive until its fence.

Staying GPU modified does not bring a read to those images. They have forced_flushed set, so
GetFlushArea makes the area preemtive and OnCPURead returns with no flush: that is what the fence
download was for. On a Switch 2 title with no fastmem arena a read of a page without its GPU written
mark does not even ask, and only the buffer cache marks pages. A core may also keep the area of an
earlier read until the read trap generation moves. FlushOnNextRead clears all three. The generation
moves at most once in 250 ms, the length of the pool's pause, so that a large image that is refused
again does not cost a GPU thread round trip for every word the guest reads.

DownloadImageIntoBuffer still does the GPU copy into the buffer. Only the extra copy for guest
memory goes, and ObtainBuffer has marked that range as written. The request moves above the slot
insert so a refusal leaves nothing behind.

TextureCache::DownloadMemory is not here: on the console vulkan_download_batch.inc returns before
that loop. The fork patch handles it, and needs ReservedDownloadBuffer and FlushOnNextRead from this
one: land them in one commit.

The whole-image branch of PopAsyncFlushes is left too: IMPLEMENTS_ASYNC_DOWNLOADS is true for
Vulkan, so it is not built.

